{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792604043,"nonce":"kfzQ7gaicwVHEvjsQ3nLz2oLQUw=","message":"Implemented independent data paths: a lazy Problems worker decodes LSP diagnostics and owns fallback compiler requests, I/O and JSON parsing; Output normalizes bounded channel snapshots on a separate worker and build/run jobs own process startup/log reads on background workers; terminal PTY/process startup now uses a native worker, alongside the existing reader/parser worker. UI polls only while requests are outstanding. Diagnostic requests coalesce per file, cancelled/superseded results are discarded, idle workers release their last task, and disposal does not join workers. Output keeps one active and one latest pending snapshot per channel, so continuous logs still update the view. Terminal input arriving during startup is bounded and queued.\n\nProblems mounts a viewport plus overscan (24 rows at the probe size), with full-height spacers and source navigation. Hidden Output unmounts its controls, keeping CodeEditorState text/scroll data and stable highlighters; hidden logs do not rebuild it. Severity regexes are precompiled. Profile menus build only when opened. The closed-panel attribute is now on the resize handle, avoiding CSS invalidation of the editor ancestor subtree. Adopted Ashui 70e0aa6b35dd304e7690a3e0b92be83bdd126d1b for stable editor row slots and cached visible document width. Show Output waits for worker delivery before revealing the latest message.\n\nMeasurement: tests/PanelLatencyProbe.hx, hybrid Ash application preset, 1280x800, 2,000-field source, 200 diagnostics and 10,000 output lines. No PNG readback in timed frames. Compare bin/panel-latency-before.log and bin/panel-latency-final.log. Values below are the slowest frame of each transition, not action-handler time or universal latency guarantees. The initial baseline Output view had already processed its log while hidden; the new initial Output mounts on demand.\n\nFirst open: Problems 1273.6 -\u003e 106.7 ms, Output 171.1 -\u003e 110.0 ms, Terminal 367.0 -\u003e 93.8 ms.\nWarm opens, cycles 1-2: Problems 570.7-572.9 -\u003e 78.0-88.2 ms; Output 138.5-222.1 -\u003e 60.2-75.1 ms; Terminal 225.1-268.0 -\u003e 49.5-59.2 ms.\nFirst Problems close: 409.5 -\u003e 85.4 ms. Warm close frames across panels are 76-95 ms after the changes. Problems transition allocations: about 63-66 MiB -\u003e 25 MiB. The remaining transition work is UI layout/painting, which stays on the UI thread.\n\nValidation: complete core Checks pass; worker coalescing/cancellation, LSP decoding, process output/exit, continuous log delivery and queued terminal input pass in hybrid and AOT; native terminal 7 tests pass; Ashui CodeComponents 307 checks pass; panels, basic, LSP and Git snapshots pass in both themes, including diagnostic navigation, scroll restoration, hidden Output updates, profile menus, Git notification reveal, severity eviction and selection preservation. Inspected dark/light panel screenshots. Native bin/rayde and bin/RayDE.app rebuilt successfully. No Rayzor source or compiler rebuild was performed.","files":null}]}